    <p class=3D"paragraph-elevate inline-placeholder vossi-paragraph_elevat=
e" data-uri=3D"cms.cnn.com/_components/paragraph/instances/paragraph-497b41=
82e266f64ea55f77facd28621e@published" data-editable=3D"text" data-component=
-name=3D"paragraph" data-article-gutter=3D"true">
            In a world that all too often tells girls =E2=80=93 especially =
black girls =E2=80=93 that they don=E2=80=99t belong in STEM, Katherine Joh=
nson was exactly the icon our girls needed. In a world where black women ma=
ke up <a href=3D"https://www.ncwit.org/resources/ncwit-scorecard-status-wom=
en-computing-2019-update" target=3D"_blank">just 13% of computer scientists=
</a>, Katherine was a visible role model and a reminder that we need more.=
=20
    </p><div class=3D"quantum-wrapper ad-slot-wrapper qtm-element  is-ad-re=
design" data-ad-label-text=3D"Advertisement" data-ad-id=3D"ad_multi_atf_02"=
