    <p class=3D"paragraph-elevate inline-placeholder vossi-paragraph_elevat=
e" data-uri=3D"cms.cnn.com/_components/paragraph/instances/paragraph-452880=
9fc45d6c156e5eb3b9c7d1724c@published" data-editable=3D"text" data-component=
-name=3D"paragraph" data-article-gutter=3D"true">
            And we should celebrate her, most of all, for her bravery. I ta=
lk a lot about how women are conditioned to be perfect, and how by embracin=
g bravery we could accomplish so much more. Katherine was the epitome of br=
avery. When <a href=3D"https://www.nasa.gov/audience/foreducators/a-lifetim=
e-of-stem.html" target=3D"_blank">she was told</a> that women didn=E2=80=99=
t participate in the briefings at NASA; she asked whether there was a law a=
gainst it. There wasn=E2=80=99t. So Katherine started attending briefings. =
She asked questions. She, bravely, put herself in the rooms where she knew =
she deserved to be. =20
    </p><div class=3D"quantum-wrapper ad-slot-wrapper qtm-element  is-ad-re=
design" data-ad-label-text=3D"Advertisement" data-ad-id=3D"ad_multi_atf_03"=
 data-ad-position=3D"desktop">
    <div class=3D"qtm-slot-inner ad-qtm" data-ad-text=3D"show" data-ad-refr=
esh=3D"adbody" id=3D"ad_multi_atf_03"></div>
</div>

    <p class=3D"paragraph-elevate inline-placeholder vossi-paragraph_elevat=
e" data-uri=3D"cms.cnn.com/_components/paragraph/instances/paragraph-41390a=
1cf9b3d268a172fae1f385f181@published" data-editable=3D"text" data-component=
-name=3D"paragraph" data-article-gutter=3D"true">
            Katherine helped us see new worlds. She gave us a new perspecti=
ve on our planet, a view of earth from space. And she gave us a new perspec=
tive on ourselves: on whom we let in, whom we allow to thrive, whom we writ=
e into our history books. =20
    </p>

    <p class=3D"paragraph-elevate inline-placeholder vossi-paragraph_elevat=
e" data-uri=3D"cms.cnn.com/_components/paragraph/instances/paragraph-37d7e9=
32f300cfaba4626c7295636fc4@published" data-editable=3D"text" data-component=
-name=3D"paragraph" data-article-gutter=3D"true">
            Katherine, <a href=3D"https://www.nasa.gov/feature/katherine-jo=
hnson-the-girl-who-loved-to-count" target=3D"_blank">you once said</a>, =E2=
=80=9CI counted everything. I counted the steps to the road, the steps up t=
o church, the number of dishes and silverware I washed =E2=80=A6 anything t=
hat could be counted, I did.=E2=80=9D =20
    </p>

